<% content_for :title, "About | Star Wars Explorer" %>

<h1 class="mb-4">About This Project</h1>

<div class="row">
  <div class="col-lg-6">
    <h2>Data Source</h2>
    <p>
      All data comes from the <a href="https://swapi.dev">Star Wars API (SWAPI)</a>,
      a free JSON API that needs no key. Five endpoints are used:
      <strong>people</strong>, <strong>planets</strong>, <strong>species</strong>,
      <strong>starships</strong> and <strong>vehicles</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>How the Data Is Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Each person has one homeworld; a planet has many people (one-to-many).</li>
      <li>A person may belong to a species; a species has many people (one-to-many).</li>
      <li>People pilot many starships, and starships have many pilots (many-to-many through <code>starship_pilots</code>).</li>
      <li>People pilot many vehicles, and vehicles have many pilots (many-to-many through <code>vehicle_pilots</code>).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How It Was Imported</h2>
    <p>
      The seed script downloads every page of each endpoint. The API links records
      with URLs, so the script uses those URLs to find the matching records and
      creates the relationships with Active Record's own IDs.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="col-lg-6">
    <h2>Database Diagram (ERD)</h2>
    <%= image_tag "erd.png", alt: "Entity relationship diagram of the Star Wars Explorer database", class: "img-fluid border rounded" %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row mt-4">
  <div class="col-12">
    <h2>Site Features</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Paginated lists of people, planets, species, starships and vehicles.</li>
      <li>Detail pages that link between related records (e.g. a person and their homeworld).</li>
      <li>Search people by name and filter by homeworld.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
